# Allowlist: exclude everything, then include only what Containerfiles need.
*

# Go workspace
!go.work
!go.work.sum

# Go components (full source for those that are cross-module dependencies)
!fulfillment-service/
!bare-metal-fulfillment-operator/
!osac-operator/
!osac-csi-driver/
!osac-metering/
!osac-ui/

# osac-observability: the helper binaries (remote-write-config, query-allowlist,
# admin-credentials, query-auth-gate) are built from this module by its own
# Containerfile, which the installer Makefile and the publish workflow build
# with the repository root as the context. Without this entry the allowlist
# above filters the module out and the build fails at COPY go.mod.
!osac-observability/

# osac-aap: ansible-builder execution-environment component, built from a
# hand-maintained Containerfile (see osac-aap/Containerfile's own header
# comment) rather than one generated live by a custom Tekton task.
!osac-aap/

# Shared proto module: every Containerfile now COPYs proto/ for the single
# generated Go tree at proto/gen/ that all components import.
!proto/

# Standalone CaaS simulator: allow this module without other integration data.
!tests/
tests/*
!tests/integration/
tests/integration/*
!tests/integration/caas/
tests/integration/caas/go.work.sum

# Conformance suite image: setuptools reads the root build metadata and the
# packaged tests. Both are excluded by the allowlist above.
!pyproject.toml
!tests/
